<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.4.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00907</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.4.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ccdfa7b6-f7f9-48ac-8e68-5307c03d56db</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<section id="sect-00002"><exercise id="_3b03d196-7526-4071-b198-999c2e4d4c08" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00001"><para id="para-00002">Match each equation with a verbal description that represents the same function.</para>
      <para id="para-00003">\(f(x)=2x+4\)</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00001"><para id="para-00004">Correct!  To get the output, multiply the input by 2, then add 4 to the result.</para><para id="para-00005">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2.</para><para id="para-00006">The correct answer is to get the output, multiply the input by 2, then add 4 to the result.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_234da651-94df-4ff5-af49-007f3ed47257" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00002"><para id="para-00007">\(g(x)=2(x+4) \)</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00002"><para id="para-00008">Correct!  To get the output, add 4 to the input, then multiply the result by 2.</para><para id="para-00009">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2.</para><para id="para-00010">The correct answer is To get the output, add 4 to the input, then multiply the result by 2 <emphasis>.</emphasis></para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="bf984679-4679-4e9b-bd3b-85ae0fd95e57" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00003"><para id="para-00011">\(h(x)=4x+2\)</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00003"><para id="para-00012">Correct!  To get the output, multiply the input by 4, then add 2 to the result.</para><para id="para-00013">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2.</para><para id="para-00014">The correct answer is to get the output, multiply the input by 4, then add 2 to the result.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_5955ed6d-6f72-4398-bb5d-80cb2b9881a9" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00004"><para id="para-00015">\(k(x)=4(x+2)\)</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00004"><para id="para-00016">Correct!  To get the output, add 2 to the input, then multiply the result by 4.</para><para id="para-00017">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2.</para><para id="para-00018">The correct answer is To get the output, add 2 to the input, then multiply the result by 4.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_0d08ce71-3fc2-4a8f-a27e-c97d363f1731" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00005"><para id="para-00019">Functions \(A\) and \(B\) are defined by these equations.
          \(A(x)=25+10x\) \(B(x)=80-15x\) 
          Which function has a greater value when \(x\) is 2.5?</para>
      <para id="para-00020">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00021">\(A(x)=25+10x\)</para><para id="para-00022">\(B(x)=80-15x\)</para></problem><solution id="sol-00005"><para id="para-00023">Correct!  Function A has a greater value because B(2.5)=42.5 and A(2.5)=50.</para><para id="para-00024">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.3.</para><para id="para-00025">The correct answer is Function A has a greater value because \(B(2.5)=42.5\) and \(A(2.5)=50\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_998043ad-68ac-4dc6-b932-88437166f755" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00006"><para id="para-00026">Which function is greater when \(x = 4\)?</para>
      <para id="para-00027">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00028">\(f(x)=2x-7\)</para><para id="para-00029">\(f(x)=-3x+1\)</para><para id="para-00030">\(f(x)= -5x+2\)</para><para id="para-00031">\(f(x)=x-10\)</para></problem><solution id="sol-00006"><para id="para-00032">Correct! \(f(x)=2x -7\)</para><para id="para-00033">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2.</para><para id="para-00034">The correct answer is \(f(x)=2x -7\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="a6cbad77-b6a6-46d6-9940-8b2019b175a9" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00007"><para id="para-00035">Which function rule describes the table below:</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00001">
        <tgroup cols="6"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              \(x\)
           </emphasis> </entry><entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
            <entry>
              5
            </entry>
            <entry>
              6
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              \(y\)
           </emphasis> </entry><entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              5
            </entry>
            <entry>
              7
            </entry>
            <entry>
              9
            </entry>
            <entry>
              11
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      
    <para id="para-00036">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00037">\(f(x)=x+1\)</para><para id="para-00038">\(f(x)=3x-3\)</para><para id="para-00039">\(f(x)=2x-1\)</para><para id="para-00040">\(f(x)=x+2\)</para></problem><solution id="sol-00007"><para id="para-00041">Correct! \(f(x)=2x-1\)</para><para id="para-00042">Try again. Revisit activities 4.4.3.</para><para id="para-00043">The correct answer is \(f(x)=2x-1\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_5ea74f7e-7211-4aa4-ae4f-db4b69b5ad08" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00008"><para id="para-00044">Write a function \(g(x)\) for the following statement: to get the output, subtract 4 from the input, then multiply the result by 2.</para>
      <para id="para-00045">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00046">\(g(x)=2x-4\)</para><para id="para-00047">\(g(x)=-4-2x\)</para><para id="para-00048">\(g(x)=x -8\)</para><para id="para-00049">\(g(x)=2(x-4)\)</para></problem><solution id="sol-00008"><para id="para-00050">Correct! \(g(x)=2(x-4)\)</para><para id="para-00051">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.1.</para><para id="para-00052">The correct answer is \(g(x)=2(x-4)\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="ad08a7ed-c590-4281-852d-11570c6bce38" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00009"><para id="para-00053">Write a function \(h(x)\) for the following statement: to get the output, multiply the input by 5 and then add 2.</para>
      <para id="para-00054">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00055">\(h(x)=5(x+2)\)</para><para id="para-00056">\(h(x)=5x+2\)</para><para id="para-00057">\(h(x)=x +2(5)\)</para><para id="para-00058">\(h(x)=x+2\)</para></problem><solution id="sol-00009"><para id="para-00059">Correct! \(h(x)=5x+2\)</para><para id="para-00060">Try again. Revisit activities 4.4.1.</para><para id="para-00061">The correct answer is \(h(x)=5x+2\).</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="c60f5cda-248c-45f1-b8d8-19fc43601821" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00010"><para id="para-00062">Find the value of \(f(x)=−2x−3\) when \(x=2\).</para>
      <para id="para-00063">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00064">7</para><para id="para-00065">1</para><para id="para-00066">-1</para><para id="para-00067">-7</para></problem><solution id="sol-00010"><para id="para-00068">Correct! -7</para><para id="para-00069">Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2.</para><para id="para-00070">The correct answer is -7.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="e067d2ce-4e9a-4fe3-87c3-6fbb16068c95" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00011"><para id="para-00071">Examine the table below. Find \(g(2.5)\) using the rule for this table.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00002">
        <tgroup cols="5"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              \(x\)
           </emphasis> </entry><entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis>
              \(g(x)\)
           </emphasis> </entry><entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              6
            </entry>
            <entry>
              10
            </entry>
            <entry>
              14
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      
    </problem><solution id="sol-00011"><para id="para-00072">Correct! \(g(x)=4x-2\), \(g(2.5)=8\)</para><para id="para-00073">Try again. Revisit activities 4.4.4.</para><para id="para-00074">The correct answer is \(g(x)=4x-2\), \(g(2.5)=8\).</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content></document>